# ── Simulator ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UDID, name, or the literal `booted`. Unset means "the only booted simulator";
# two booted and no value is an error that names them, rather than the coin flip
# simctl's own `booted` performs.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_ID=C4AB4BE0-C0BC-436C-8C03-8F87330DFFA5

# ── Safety ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Writes are ON by default — the one place this server differs from the rest of
# the fleet. A simulator is disposable and holds no real person's data, so the
# reasoning that keeps mcp-ios-device read-only does not carry over. Set this to
# 0 to drop the fourteen driving tools from tools/list entirely (not refuse them
# — remove them), leaving five read-only ones.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_ALLOW_WRITES=0

# Prepended to every ios_simulator_launch that does not pass its own arguments.
# Point the app at fixtures rather than whatever it opens by default.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_LAUNCH_ARGS=-DemoMode -NoCloud

# ── WebDriverAgent ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the UI tree and the input tools need it. Screenshots go through simctl and
# work with nothing installed.
#
# One port per simulator, always. A simulator shares this Mac's network stack, so
# the runner's port is a host port — and WebDriverAgent scans 8100-8199 when
# USE_PORT is unset, which means a second simulator's runner comes up healthy on
# 8101 and a server pointed at 8100 drives the *first* simulator while every call
# reports success. ios_simulator_diagnostics reports the port's real owner.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_WDA_PORT=8100
# IOS_SIMULATOR_WDA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8100

# ── Tuning ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Budget for one simctl call. A cold boot or a large install is slow.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# IOS_SIMULATOR_WDA_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Byte cap on an ios_simulator_ui_tree payload.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_MAX_TREE_BYTES=24000
# Where saved screenshots, launch logs and the runner log land.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_OUTPUT_DIR=/tmp/mcp-ios-simulator
# Log every simctl and WebDriverAgent call to stderr.
# IOS_SIMULATOR_DEBUG=1

# ── Toolchain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IOS_SIMULATOR_XCRUN_PATH=/usr/bin/xcrun
# IOS_SIMULATOR_SIPS_PATH=/usr/bin/sips
# IOS_SIMULATOR_PLUTIL_PATH=/usr/bin/plutil
# IOS_SIMULATOR_OPEN_PATH=/usr/bin/open
